+// May this configuration carry the TWO-ARM pair (a prefill arm and a decode arm on ONE llama_memory)?
+//
+// PURE apart from ONE GGUF metadata key: no state change, no allocation, so the reservation derivation and the
+// server call the SAME function and cannot disagree -- a pair that is refused after the reserve was charged
+// leaves the MoE arena several GiB smaller for a context that is never created (defect V2 of DESIGN.md).  The
+// exception is `general.architecture` of a specified draft model: a gemma4 assistant shares the TARGET's KV and
+// is not distinguishable from an admitted `draft-simple`/`draft-mtp` by anything in `common_params` (see
+// common_speculative_path_shares_target_kv()), and refusing it after the load would reintroduce exactly V2.
+//
+// Returns nullptr when the pair is possible, else a one-line REASON suitable for the log.  The refusals are
+// properties of the SHAPE (they do not depend on the request): a second context with its own batch, ubatch,
+// scheduler and compute buffers cannot serve a multimodal input pipeline, a TTS/realtime loop, an
+// embedding/rerank/decision request, a LoRA stack, the idle-sleep state machine or a backend sampler, and a
+// drafter whose TARGET side is bound to one context (the layer-input families, and a gemma4 assistant that
+// shares the target's KV) assumes it is the only other user of that context.
+const char * common_arms_pair_possible(const common_params & params);
+
 // apply --fit to mparams and cparams, no-op if params.fit_params is false
 void common_fit_apply(common_params & params, struct llama_model_params & mparams, struct llama_context_params & cparams);
 
@@ -1280,6 +1316,12 @@ struct common_batch {
